    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:</i>&nbsp;<i><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Threats_of_the_Galaxy\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy\">Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy</a></i> </p><p>A Mandalorian Jet Pack functions identically to a standard <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Jet_Pack\" title=\"Jet Pack\">Jet Pack</a>, but has an integrated <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Missile_Launcher\" title=\"Missile Launcher\">Missile Launcher</a> and a magnetic grappling hook (which functions as a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Liquid_Cable_Dispenser\" title=\"Liquid Cable Dispenser\">Liquid Cable Dispenser</a>). A Mandalorian Jet Pack is considered to have a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Military\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Military\">Military</a> availability. Replacement fuel cells cost 100 credits. </p><p>Activating a Mandalorian Jet Pack is a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Swift_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Swift Action\">Swift Action</a>, and you gain a fly speed of 6 squares until the end of your turn. A Mandalorian Jet Pack has 10 charges and can be run continuously; no <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Swift_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Swift Action\">Swift Action</a> is required to activate the Mandalorian Jet Pack on subsequent rounds of use. </p><p>Routine maneuvers do not require a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pilot\" title=\"Pilot\">Pilot</a> check, but you must make a DC 20 <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pilot\" title=\"Pilot\">Pilot</a> check if you land after moving more than 12 squares during the same turn; on a failure you fall <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Prone\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Prone\">Prone</a>. </p>",
